Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: more gaps of an analytic blend run over holes and cut by the face
beyond (0055, mitcad#121): e.g. the rim of a cylinder whose top is crossed
by blind holes or by notches open to a bore, or a circle on a cone's base
whose contact on a ledge crosses round notches.

- ChFi3d_FillKPartGaps: the pieces of a closed spine are taken in the
  order of their starts. SplitKPart cuts the piece across the spine's
  start in two and lists them first, so the gaps next to that start were
  not between consecutive pieces and were left to the walking.
- ChFi3d_KPartCutPiece: of the face beyond's vertices, only those on its
  boundary with the face the contact leaves count as lying under the blend
  (an edge of the face beyond ending there would have to be prolonged).
  Before, the vertex at the bottom of a blind hole refused the cut.
- ChFi3d_KPartCutCurve: on an intersection line that closes on itself
  without being periodic, the arc from one end of the cut to the other
  that runs across the line's ends is tried too (joined into one B-spline),
  and a point at an end of a line counts as on it; the arcs are checked to
  lie across the blend by their 3d points.
- ChFi3d_FillKPartGaps: where the cut is no single line from one end to
  the other but two lines that meet (the intersection is split where a
  surface's parameter wraps), the gap is filled with two pieces split at
  the section through the point where the lines meet
  (ChFi3d_KPartCutJunction), not at the gap's middle.
